			<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

			<details class="mt-5 border-b border-border pb-4">
				<summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary">How do online gaming platforms process games in real time?</summary>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
					Your in-game actions are packaged by the app into an API request and sent over your internet connection to the platform's server. The server validates the action, updates the game state in the database, and sends back a response. For interactive multiplayer games, WebSocket connections keep a persistent channel open between your device and the server so updates are pushed instantly without waiting for your app to ask. The entire round trip typically takes under 200 milliseconds on a stable connection.
				</p>
			</details>

			<details class="mt-5 border-b border-border pb-4">
				<summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary">Are online gaming platforms like Comegame safe for Indian users?</summary>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
					Reputable platforms use end-to-end encryption for data in transit, encrypted storage for sensitive data at rest, OTP-based authentication, KYC to verify identities, and anti-fraud systems running continuously in the background. User-side security practices are equally important: never share your OTP, use a unique password, and keep the app updated. Download the app only from official sources — the <a href="/download-come-games-app" class="text-primary underline-offset-4 hover:underline">official Comegame download page</a> is the right starting point.
				</p>
			</details>

			<details class="mt-5 border-b border-border pb-4">
				<summary class="cursor-pointer text-base font-semibold text-foreground hover:text-primary">How do gaming platforms ensure fairness in skill games?</summary>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">
					In skill games like fantasy cricket, outcomes depend on actual real-world sports performance and the player's team selection decisions — the platform does not control the cricket match. Where randomness is involved (such as card shuffling), certified RNG algorithms ensure unbiased, unpredictable outputs. Game logic runs server-side, meaning no player can modify the app on their device to change the outcome. Consistent rules, certified scoring algorithms, and anti-collusion monitoring create equal conditions for all participants.
				</p>
